course: dictionary
lesson: 8620
title: Scribble and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: The same word can work as different parts of speech, and the sentence shows you which one. As a verb, scribble means to write or draw quickly and carelessly. «The Rat was scribbling poetry» shows the Rat writing fast, not neatly.
explain: As a noun, a scribble is messy writing or a messy drawing of lines. Ruby in Glasgow says her wee (little) brother «scribbled on it», so she binned it. Here the marks are messy lines that spoil the page, so scribbled is the verb and the marks are the noun.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Nia's name label says «OLIVIA P», so she scribbles it out. Scribbling it out means covering the name with messy lines so no one can read it. To check any meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Scribble can be a verb (to scribble) or a noun (a scribble).
fact: «Scribble» as a verb means to write or draw quickly and carelessly.
fact: «A scribble» means messy writing or a messy drawing of lines.
fact: «Scribble down» means write something quickly, as in «scribble a note».
fact: «Wee» (Scotland) means little.
exercise: «...soon the Rat is scribbling poetry: the cure has begun.» What is the Rat doing? | *Writing poetry quickly and carelessly | Sleeping under a tree | Painting a picture of the harvest | Reading a long book
exercise: Ruby says her wee brother scribbled on the paper, so she binned it. What did the brother do? | Tidied the paper neatly | Folded it into a paper boat | Read the paper aloud | *Made messy marks on the paper
exercise: Find the word that means messy writing or a messy drawing of lines. | Cosy | Tactful | *Scribble | Harvest
test:
Nia scribbles out «OLIVIA P» on her jumper label. What does she do? | *Covers the name with messy lines | Sews a new label on the jumper | Reads the name out loud | Sends the jumper back to the swap box
test:
Which phrase means to write something down quickly? | *Scribble down | Scribble on the wall | Tactful Mole | Cosy winter
exam:
In «the Rat was scribbling and sucking the top of his pencil», what does scribbling mean? | *Writing quickly and carelessly | Eating a snack | Singing a song | Sleeping near the fire
